    "knowledge_point": "Finding Exact Values of Trigonometric Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula",
    "problem": "Find the exact value of $1-2{sin}^{2}⁡({22.5}^{∘}).$",
    "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={22.5}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2{sin}^{2}⁡({22.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {22.5}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
